==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{m|frm|avec}}, {{m|frm|avecques||with}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|avoc}}, {{m|fro|avoec}}, {{m|fro|avuec||with}}, from an assumed {{etyl|LL.|fr}} {{m|la|*aboc}}, {{m|la|*abhoc}}, {{m|la|*apud hŏque}}<ref>"Brachet, ''An etymological dictionary of the French language'', avec.</ref><ref name=a>http://www.cnrtl.fr/etymologie/avec</ref>, a Frankish alteration consisting of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|apud||with, near, close to}} with {{m|la|hoc||this}} and {{m|la|-que}}. First used as a replacement for {{cog|la|cum||with}} in [[w:Merovingian|Merovingian]] and [[w:Carolingian|Carolingian]] (Frankish) documents. Gradually supplanted Old French {{m|fro|od||with}}, itself from {{m|la|apud}}.<ref name=a/> Cognate with Picard {{m|pcd|aveuc}}, Norman {{m|nrm|aveu}}, Walloon {{m|wa|avou}} and Franco-Provençal: {{m|frp|avouéc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|Fr-avec.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}

===Preposition===
{{fr-prep}}

# {{qualifier|accompaniment}} [[with]]
#: {{ux|fr|Je suis revenu '''avec''' lui.|t=I have returned '''with''' him.}}
# {{qualifier|manner, instrument}} [[with]]

